    "notOk": [
      "F5: the close budgets are one formula and a table that never answers rejects at exactly the stated bound",
      "F7: a process that is still exiting at the confirming table is re-read once after a bounded settle and reported as exiting, not as a survivor",
      "F7: a process that never leaves stays a survivor after the single re-read, and the re-read sends no further kill",
      "F7: a re-read that fails keeps the survivors, records the failure and never claims clean",
      "F7: exitSettleMs is validated like every other duration",
      "SR5: the outcome of a close is ONE deep-frozen value: nothing a caller does to it changes what the next caller of the shared close() receives",
      "SR5: the CloseError of an unclean close is frozen as well and shares nothing with the tree report it was built from",
      "SR7: options that are not an object are a typed refusal before anything runs, and a missing options argument means the defaults",
      "SR7: an option whose getter throws is a typed refusal that names the option",
      "SR7: every close option is read exactly once, so a getter cannot pass the check and then deliver another value",
      "F1: two live sessions opened through openLessonSession, closed first then second: each close ends only its own browser",
      "F1: a graceful close that leaves its own tree behind ends that tree by identity and never the browser of another live session",
      "F2: close() during the baseline read ends the startup at once: nothing is launched and no virtual time passes",
      "F2: close() while the startup is queued behind another startup does not wait for the lock holder",
      "F3: every real test closes the sessions it opens in a finally block and asserts the root and a lower bound, never that every recorded process is alive",
      "F3: a failing assertion inside a guarded real test still closes the sessions it opened (the cleanup ran)",
      "SR5: the outcome of a close during a failed startup is a frozen copy: nothing a caller does to it is visible to the next failed startup",
      "SR7: a signal that is not an AbortSignal, or whose getter throws, is a typed refusal before the opener is called"
